pokemon has ballooned into an incredible  essential franchise you simply can't  imagine what your life would have been  like without it particularly in the  early gen 1 days of the red and green  versions or blue version for those of us  outside of japan there are many minor  interesting details about pokemon that  fans may not know or have forgotten  about despite many infamous exploits  like the missing number glitch so here  are 10 pokemon things that you might not  have known about pokemon if you want  more pokemon sub to this channel as the  latest game legends arceus is fast  approaching and will have plenty of  coverage when it releases  one of the best parts of playing pokemon  whether it's the video game or the card  game is the concept of collecting as  much as you can there are hundreds of  different pokemon species just waiting  to be caught so it makes sense that the  inspiration for pokemon also came from a  similar hobby insect collecting that's  right the original concept of the  pokemon came from satoshi tajiri one of  the creators of game freak and his hobby  of insect collecting as a child combined  with the fascination of the gameboy's  link cable he even described imagining  little bugs crawling through the cables  between game boys at one point  when deciding which platform to develop  pokemon on the gameboy's link cable was  the deciding factor for todri fueled by  a frustrating encounter with the dragon  quest 2 item on the famicom tajiri  desperately wanted a hard to find item  from dragon quest and try to find a way  to acquire the item from fellow pokemon  creator ken sugamori who happened to  have two but to no avail since the  famicom had no way to connect two games  thus we have the inspiration for  utilizing the gameboy's link cable to  trade pokemon with friends nintendo at  first couldn't grasp the concept of  using the link cable to trade  collectibles or the appeal of pokemon in  general still they trusted tajiri's game  development reputation and decided to  give it a shot the rest as they say is  history  most fans of pokemon know that pokemon  is short for pocket monsters indicated  by trainers stashing away pokeballs  they've used to catch any given pokemon  in their literal pocket what's less  known is that this wasn't tajiri's first  choice for the name instead he hoped to  call the game capsule monsters but ran  into trademark issues shortening capsule  monsters to capmon didn't quite hit the  same mark either and the name eventually  found a home in pokemon  alright if i were to ask you which  pokemon was first created maybe you'd  say pikachu since pikachu is arguably  the most recognizable pokemon of all  time or you might say bulbasaur since  its national pokedex number is literally  zero zero one arguments can also be made  for charizard or venusaur as the covers  for red and green but in actuality the  first pokemon designed was ride-on ride  on might not be number one of the  national decks but according to ken  sugimori its internal id number is one  it makes sense too since you'll see the  ride on sprite a lot throughout gen 1  whether in pokemon gym statues or as  sprites for other pokemon when in your  team menus  one of the most iconic secrets was mew a  pokemon after the legendary mewtwo to  fully appreciate how incredible the  mythical mew was you had to be a kid  growing up in the mid 90s honestly mew  was like this playground folklore  something you'd hear about at the park  and it added to the mystique of gen 1.  the way mew was integrated into the  cartridge is just as surprising because  nintendo had no clue since game freak  simply popped mew in at the very end of  the development process mew couldn't be  found in the game without exploiting a  glitch or cheating but that didn't stop  trainers from doing what they needed to  do to catch mew and add it to their team  eventually mew was distributed to select  few trainers officially and a growing  trend of special events were established  in future games players would gather at  these events and get special mystery  gift pokemon or items many of which  included mythical pokemon like mew  arguably one of the biggest positives of  playing gold silver and crystal is that  the gen 2 games let you explore kanto  from gen 1 after you became champion as  a kid this was an incredible experience  before ending in a climactic battle  against red in mount silver what fans  probably don't know is that the kanto  region almost didn't make the cut in gen  2 after all kanto is a vast region which  means a lot of data for the game boy  hardware cramming both johto and kanto  onto the same cartridge was no small  task it was nearly impossible that is  until satoru iwata who later became the  president of nintendo showed gamefreak a  way to compress the data to be  manageable there are story implications  for why kanto appears sparse in certain  areas but we have a technical  explanation as well which is why areas  like viridian forest are dramatically  different in gen 2. either way game  freak owed a lot to mystery iwata and  there's even a heartwarming easter egg  later an ultra moon and ultra sun  referencing mr iwata's role during gen  2's development  the game corner is notorious for several  reasons especially in gens 1 and 2. for  starters it posed as team rocket's  original hideout in celadon city that  same game corner was also the only way  to get a porygon in the game for a cool  9999 coins but really the game corners  were known for one thing being a  glorified casino yeah you could spend  in-game money to acquire coins to then  bet on the slot machines next to npcs to  then use your winnings for everything  from pokemon to rare and powerful tms  the game corner appeared in gens 2 3 and  4 but with pokemon platinum things got a  little weird specifically for south  korea and europe around this time onward  anti-gambling laws in those countries  grew more strict the rating systems were  no longer going to give pokemon a  kid-friendly rating so to help avoid any  raiding above an e the casinos were  removed from future games including the  gen 2 and 3 remakes  yeah whooper is based on a real life  animal you'd think most pokemon are  right for example butterfree and  beedrill are based on their obvious  insect in real life counterparts but  still things get strange when you have  water tortoises like blastoise with  literal water cannons however whooper is  based on the water-based salamander  called an axolotl straight up who would  have guessed  so gen 2 actually had a demo that not a  lot of folks remember there's sparse  footage of it online but one of the  cooler concepts is that the protagonist  of gen 2 gold actually had a skateboard  instead of a bike the footage shows gold  clipping through various map parts which  is clearly a bug but the interesting  thing is that he's also popping ollies  on the skateboard potentially meant to  be able to jump back up from ledges or  to reach hard to obtain spaces of course  the skateboard never made it to the  final cut and instead we got the gen 1  standard bike that players were  accustomed to funny enough later on in  the ruby sapphire versions we see the  acro bike which lets you pop wheelies  and hop around so the inspiration for  having spots that you could only reach  with the key item was kind of always  there the skateboard also actually has a  canonical tie-in as gold is shown riding  a skateboard in the pokemon manga  alright so this one was my favorite  because of just how bonkers it was and  just how ridiculous at the time but it's  absolutely true and newer pokemon fans  you guys might not be aware of it but in  the pokemon anime an episode was banned  for giving nearly 700 japanese kids  seizures yeah in the episode in question  pikachu uses a thunderbolt on a bunch of  missiles from a porygon that when they  collided caused an incredibly rapid  strobe effect of red and blue lights  flashing in a dizzying manner almost  immediately viewers at home reported  headaches nausea and full-on seizures  that required hospitalization almost  recklessly even more viewers had  seizures later when newscasts literally  replayed the scene during their  broadcast when reporting on the seizures  which you'd think they'd know better but  here we are just doesn't get more ironic  than that thankfully the episode was  pulled from airwaves almost immediately  and has never been broadcast again  alright so there's 10 things you didn't  know about pokemon or probably didn't  maybe you knew all of this already and  are super smart or something i don't  know pokemon legends rcs is rapidly  approaching though and we're excited for  the game coming so soon if you're a  veteran pokemon fan let me know in the  comments your best pokemon trivia that  fans might not know and if you're new to  the series let me know if there's  anything you're excited about for  pokemon be sure to check out our  upcoming legends rcs videos and  subscribe to gamespot for all things  gaming until next time  [Music]  you
 

